.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-OVERVIEW 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-overview
.Nd one screen of what this machine is running
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints, once, what this machine has and what it is running: the kldload
version, distribution, kernel, cores, memory and uptime; each pool's size
and use, and how many datasets and snapshots there are; every virtual
machine and its state; Podman containers; whether a Kubernetes cluster is
up; the GPU's temperature, power and memory; the addresses of the main
interfaces; the eBPF tools present; and whether the core services are
running.
It ends with the commands that go further.
A section that has nothing to show \(em no cluster, no GPU, no containers
\(em says so or is left out; none makes the whole report fail.
.Pp
It runs itself under
.Xr sudo 8 ,
since the virtual machines and some services can only be read as root.
It changes nothing.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print what it shows and exit 0.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0.
